# Window W2 of the ACPI specification (§7.4) on a recorded machine: the initialisation of the namespace of the MSI
# MS-7E16, an AMD client, steps 2 to 9 of §3.8, inside the ring-0 corpus test the_boot_module_machine_loads, on a
# debug server kernel (./build.sh --server). The boot runs the same function on q35's own tables first, hence skip=1.
# tools/acpi/corpus.sh module 'Desktop/MSI/MS-7/MS-7E16/B75C85853132' writes the module. The corpus test tells firmware
# the APIC model, the MADT declaring an I/O APIC: step 5 calls its \_PIC (1), which rewrites the PIRQ routers, 106,632
# instructions of these. Checked by
# tools/instructions.sh --budget tools/budgets/acpi-initialization-ms-7e16.debug.budget kernel/lpl.kernel; a change that moves
# the count records the new one.
inside=advanced_configuration_and_power_interface_initialize_namespace
skip=1
times=1
machine=q35
append=lpl.test=advanced_configuration_and_power_interface_corpus.the_boot_module_machine_loads
module=build/acpi-corpus/modules/Desktop_MSI_MS-7_MS-7E16_B75C85853132.acpi
instructions=2455740
accesses=1191976
tolerance=1
